{#- CYCLIST CORE, v1 — English sibling of /members/core-ciclista/. Same circuit,
    same structure; only the copy changes.

    Original note follows.

    CYCLIST CORE, v1 — built Aug 13, 2026 from Iván's `Deep core for cyclists.md`.
    Home doc: `cyclist-core-brief.md`. Third artifact on the strength engine.

    ONE question (3 or 4 rounds). Bodyweight only, on Iván's call.

    *** Rounds are rendered as PHASES — "Vuelta 1", "Vuelta 2", … — which is why
    this needs no engine change. strength-tool.js walks phases in order and shows
    the phase name in the header, so the athlete sees which round they are in for
    free. The alternative (teaching the engine about rounds) would have been a
    second concept doing the same job as the one it already has. ***

    Rest is carried on the exercises: 15s between exercises inside a round (the
    engine rests AFTER an exercise's last set), and 75s on the last exercise of
    each round, which is the rest between rounds.

    Four changes from Iván's source doc, three of them his picks:
      - thoracic rotation added to the warm-up (cyclists lose it on the bars)
      - plank shoulder taps → BEAR plank shoulder taps (hip angle nearer the bike)
      - hollow body hold → long-lever plank (hollow rehearses the flexed hip and
        thorax a cyclist is already stuck in; same anti-extension, no fault)
      - pull-through → cross-body plank reach, because bodyweight-only was the call
    OFFERED AND NOT TAKEN: a 360°/90-90 breathing and bracing entry. That is the
    "deep core" connection work, and without it this is a cycling-specific core
    routine rather than a deep-core one. Iván's decision — do not re-add it
    without asking. -#}
{% raw %}
<div class="setup" id="setup">
  <div class="crumb-bar"><div class="wrap"><a href="/members/en/#biblioteca">Library</a> / Cyclist Core</div></div>

  <div class="setup-head">
    <span class="label">Strength</span>
    <h1>Cyclist core</h1>
    <p>A cyclist's core doesn't create movement — it prevents it. Everything here trains resisting: the pelvis not rocking, the trunk not rotating, the spine not extending, while the legs push.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="setup-q">
    <div class="setup-label">How many rounds?</div>
    <div class="setup-opts" data-axis="rounds">
      <button type="button" class="setup-opt" data-val="3" aria-pressed="true">3 rounds<span>~25 min</span></button>
      <button type="button" class="setup-opt" data-val="4" aria-pressed="false">4 rounds<span>~33 min</span></button>
    </div>
    <p class="setup-hint">Three rounds is the full session. The fourth gets added once three come out with your technique intact to the end — <strong>if the hip starts rocking in the last round, that round was one too many</strong>.</p>
  </div>

  <button type="button" class="btn-primary setup-go" id="setupGo">Build my routine →</button>
</div>

<div id="toolWrap" hidden>
{% endraw %}
  {% include "partials/strength-tool.njk" %}
{% raw %}
</div>

<script>
window.CYCLIST_CORE = (function () {

  /* ---------------------------------------------------------------- LIBRARY */
  const L = {
    /* --- entrada en calor --- */
    catcow: { name: "Cat-Cow", sets: 1, reps: "10 reps", tag: "No equipment",
      cue: "On all fours, round and arch your spine with your breath. <strong>Start from the pelvis and let the spine follow one vertebra at a time</strong> — not as a block, and not just from the neck and shoulders. This is pelvic and joint control, not a stretch. Stay in a comfortable range, not end range." },
    thread: { name: "Thread the Needle", sets: 1, reps: "8 per side", tag: "No equipment",
      cue: "On all fours, slide one arm under the body until the shoulder rests, then open that same arm to the ceiling and follow it with your eyes. <strong>Hips stay still and square</strong> — the rotation comes from the mid-back, not the low back." },
    birddog: { name: "Bird Dog", sets: 1, reps: "10 per side", tag: "No equipment",
      cue: "On all fours, reach opposite arm and leg until they're in line with your torso and hold two or three seconds. <strong>Keep the hips square to the floor and the low back quiet</strong>: if a hip opens out or the back arches, lower the leg. Picture a glass of water on your low back that can't spill. Squeeze the glute as the leg reaches." },
    bridge: { name: "Glute Bridge", sets: 1, reps: "15 reps", tag: "No equipment",
      cue: "Feet close to your glutes. Drive through the heels to lift the hips and <strong>pause two seconds at the top, squeezing the glutes</strong>. The pause is the exercise; without it these are just reps. Lower with control and don't arch the low back. If you feel it in the hamstrings, slide the feet closer." },

    /* --- circuito --- */
    deadbug: { name: "Dead Bug", sets: 1, reps: "12-15 per side", rest: 15, tag: "Anti-extension",
      cue: "Lie on your back, arms to the ceiling, knees at 90°. Slowly extend opposite arm and leg without letting your lower back leave the floor. <strong>Exhale as you reach — the exhale is what pins the back down, not brute ab strength.</strong> If the low back peels up, don't lower the leg as far. This is control, not speed." },
    bearTaps: { name: "Bear Plank Shoulder Taps", sets: 1, reps: "16-20 taps", rest: 15, tag: "Anti-rotation",
      cue: "All fours, knees a few centimeters off the floor. Tap the opposite shoulder. Hips don't rock even a degree." },
    sidePlank: { name: "Side Plank with Leg Lift", sets: 1, reps: "30-40s per side", hold: 30, holdMax: 40, holdSides: 2, rest: 15, tag: "Anti-lateral-flexion",
      cue: "Forearm under the shoulder, body in a line, hips up. <strong>Once that's solid</strong>, lift and lower the top leg with control. Obliques and glute med." },
    slBridge: { name: "Single-Leg Glute Bridge", sets: 1, reps: "12-15 per leg", rest: 15, tag: "Posterior chain",
      cue: "One heel close to the glutes, other knee hugged to the chest. Drive through the heel and squeeze the glute at the top. <strong>If you feel it in the low back, tuck the pelvis and lower the height</strong>: the point is to isolate the glute, not let the psoas do the work again." },
    crossReach: { name: "Plank with Cross-Body Reach", sets: 1, reps: "10-12 reaches", rest: 15, tag: "Anti-rotation",
      cue: "High plank. Reach one hand far and across, past the other hand's line, slowly. Hips don't rotate or sag." },
    longPlank: { name: "Long-Lever Plank", sets: 1, reps: "20-30s", hold: 20, holdMax: 30, rest: 75, tag: "Anti-extension",
      cue: "Forearm plank with the elbows well ahead of the shoulders. Pelvis tucked, ribs down. Find the distance you can hold for the block without the low back sagging." },

    /* --- enfriamiento --- */
    hipflex: { name: "Half-Kneeling Hip Flexor with Glute Squeeze", sets: 1, reps: "60s per leg", hold: 60, holdSides: 2, tag: "Half-kneeling",
      cue: "Half-kneeling, front foot flat. <strong>Tuck the pelvis and squeeze the back glute hard before you shift the hip forward.</strong> Without that squeeze you're stretching the low back, not the psoas — the squeeze is the exercise." },
    child: { name: "Child's Pose", sets: 1, reps: "1-2 min", hold: 60, holdMax: 120, tag: "No equipment",
      cue: "Sit back on your heels, arms long in front, forehead to the floor. Breathe into the low back and let the hips sink a little further on each exhale. <strong>The point is to drop the revs, not to stretch farther.</strong>" }
  };

  const WARMUP  = ["catcow", "thread", "birddog", "bridge"];
  const CIRCUIT = ["deadbug", "bearTaps", "sidePlank", "slBridge", "crossReach", "longPlank"];
  const COOL    = ["hipflex", "child"];

  const WHY = "On the bike the legs produce force and the trunk has to not move. Every watt lost to a rocking pelvis or a rotating trunk is a watt that never reaches the pedal, and every hour in that position asks the core to hold without a break. That is why the whole circuit is <em>anti</em> work: anti-rotation, anti-extension, anti-lateral-flexion. There are no sit-ups here — there is a pelvis that stays still.";

  function build(rounds) {
    const pick = (ids) => ids.map((id) => {
      const e = L[id];
      if (!e) throw new Error("Unknown exercise id: " + id);
      return Object.assign({}, e);
    });

    const phases = [{ name: "Warm-up", exercises: pick(WARMUP) }];
    for (let i = 1; i <= rounds; i++) {
      phases.push({ name: "Round " + i + " of " + rounds, exercises: pick(CIRCUIT) });
    }
    phases.push({ name: "Cool-down", exercises: pick(COOL) });

    return {
      title: "Cyclist core",
      crumb: "Cyclist Core",
      kicker: "Strength",
      subtitle: "Finish each exercise and tap the button. 15 seconds between exercises; 75 at the end of each round.",
      context: rounds + " rounds · no equipment",
      why: WHY,
      warning: "<strong>Twice a week</strong>, on easy endurance days or after a ride, never before a quality session.<br><br>" +
               "<strong>Technique outranks the number.</strong> In all of these, failure is not fatigue: it is the hip starting to move. When that happens, end the set there even with reps left — a rep with the pelvis rocking trains the exact opposite of what we came here to train.",
      doneSub: "Done. You notice this in the third hour, not the first.",
      phases: phases
    };
  }

  return { build: build, library: L };
})();

/* --------------------------------------------------------------- SETUP UI */
(function () {
  const choice = { rounds: "3" };

  document.querySelectorAll(".setup-opts").forEach((group) => {
    const axis = group.dataset.axis;
    group.querySelectorAll(".setup-opt").forEach((btn) => {
      btn.addEventListener("click", () => {
        choice[axis] = btn.dataset.val;
        group.querySelectorAll(".setup-opt").forEach((b) =>
          b.setAttribute("aria-pressed", String(b === btn)));
      });
    });
  });

  document.getElementById("setupGo").addEventListener("click", () => {
    window.STRENGTH_DATA = window.CYCLIST_CORE.build(Number(choice.rounds));
    document.getElementById("setup").hidden = true;
    document.getElementById("toolWrap").hidden = false;

    const s = document.createElement("script");
    // Fingerprinted engine URL, published by the partial as TP_ENGINE_SRC.
    // A literal path here would be unfingerprinted and therefore pinned in
    // the visitor's browser for a year by Caddy's immutable header on
    // /assets/js/* — the September 8, 2026 defect. Do not inline it back.
    s.src = window.TP_ENGINE_SRC;
    document.body.appendChild(s);

    s.addEventListener("load", () => {
      const back = document.createElement("button");
      back.className = "change-link setup-back";
      back.textContent = "← Change options";
      back.addEventListener("click", () => location.reload());
      document.querySelector(".tool").prepend(back);
    });
  });
})();
</script>
{% endraw %}
